[[2,14,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The engine control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               monitors\nand controls the entire electronic ignition and injection system.</p><p>The direct supply for the system arrives\nfrom the battery from the line for the maxifuse EFI of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up\nto 2/99 or from \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from 2/99.</p><p>The control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied\ndirectly by the battery at pin 18 of connector A, via the line protected\nby fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B35</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up to 2/99 or from fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional\nfuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from 2/99.</p><p>The supply controlled by the ignition (15/54)\nreaches pin 8 of connector A, via the line protected by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B25</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up\nto 2/99 or fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from\n2/99.</p><p>Main injection relay J10 controls the entire system: this is excited by a control signal (earth) received from pin 9 of connector A of control unit M10 and then sends power:</p><ul><li>to pins 7 and 17 of connector A of the control unit, via\nthe line protected by fuse <strong>B41</strong> up to 2/99 or fuse <strong>F3</strong> of\nthe additional fuse box <strong>B98A</strong> from 2/99.;</li><li>to the injectors <strong>N70</strong> , to the air flow meter <strong>K41</strong> ,\nto the fuel vapour recovery solenoid valve <strong>L10</strong> , to the variable\nvalve timing system actuator <strong>N76</strong> and to the Lambda sensor <strong>K40</strong> ;\n(all these lines are protected by fuse <strong>B40</strong> up to 2/99 or\nfuse <strong>F2</strong> of the additional fuse box <strong>B98A</strong> from 2/99).</li></ul><p>The fuel pump relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives\na supply controlled by the ignition via fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B25</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up to 2/99\nor fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from 2/99.</p><p>It is energized by a control signal (earth)\nfrom pin 30 of connector A of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and supplies\npower to fuel pump \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N40</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , which is earthed through the inertia\nswitch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>I50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , which cuts off the circuit in the case of a crash\nand so prevents the dangerous spilling of fuel.</p><p>It also supplies power to the ignition coils\nA30.</p><p>The engine control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives\nsignals from the various sensors in order to monitor all engine\noperating parameters.</p><p>Rpm sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K46</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               provides information\non engine speed via a frequency signal sent to pins 22 and 32 of\nconnector B of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . These two signals are very\nlow intensity and are therefore shielded.</p><p>Timing sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K47</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied from\npin 29 of connector B of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and sends a signal\nof corresponding frequency to pin 23 of control unit connector B.</p><p>Engine temperature sender unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K36</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives\na reference earth from pin 1 of connector B of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and\nsupplies a signal proportional to the coolant temperature to pin\n5 of control unit connector B. The same sender unit also supplies\ninformation to the temperature gauge and warning light (\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234358\">E4023</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ).</p><p>Hot Lambda probe \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K40</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               provides control\nunit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               with information on the correct composition of the\nair-fuel mixture. The signal is sent to pin 30 of connector B of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ,\nwhile pin 21 provides a reference earth signal. Probe \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K40</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is\nheated by a resistor in order to ensure it works efficiently even\nwhen cold. The resistor is supplied by the relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and\nreceives an earth signal from pin 8 of connector B of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Knock sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               provides information\non knock status via a frequency signal sent to pin 2 of connector\nB of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . It receives a reference earth from\npin 11 of connector B. The signals are very low intensity and are\ntherefore shielded.</p><p>Air flow meter \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K41</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (supplied from\nrelay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ) receives a reference voltage from pin 1 of connector\nA and sends pin 20 of connector A a signal proportional to air flow. \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K41</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               also contains an air temperature sensor: the sensor reference\nearth is supplied by pin 29 of connector A of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , while\nan air temperature signal is received by pin 30 of connector A.</p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               controls the opening\nof individual injectors N70 via duty cycle signals produced by pins\n6 (cyl. 1), 17 (cyl. 2), 16 (cyl. 3) and 7 (cyl. 4) of connector\nB of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Injectors \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N70</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receive a power supply\nto enable opening from main relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               also controls coils \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               via\ncontrol signals (earth) for the coil primary windings, while the\nsecondary winding sends a pulse to the spark plugs: from pins 38\nand 10 of connector B for cylinder  pair 1 -4 and from pins 9 and\n37 of connector B of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               for cylinders 2-3.</p><p>The primary windings for coils \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receive\nthe supply for enabling the opening from the main relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The idle actuator \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N74</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               regulates the\nidle air flow via the butterfly. It receives a supply and reference\nearth from pins 1 and 29 of connector B of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              :\npins 4 and 13 of connector B are connected to the potentiometer\nwhich detects the position of the butterfly;  pins 26 and 35 of\nconnector B control the butterfly actuator.</p><p>Fuel vapour recovery solenoid \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>L10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               allows\nfuel vapours to pass through to the engine intake where they join\nthe mixture entering the combustion chamber. The valve \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>L10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ,\nsupplied by the main relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , is opened by the control\nunit when the engine is under load via a duty-cycle signal from\npin 34 of connector B of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The variable valve timing system \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N76</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               mechanically\ncontrols the inlet timing advance: it is controlled by pin 24 of\nconnector B of the control unit.</p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is connected to\nthe ALFA ROMEO CODE control unit via a line from pin 16 of connector\nA  (\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234721\">E7010</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ).</p><p>The control unit is equipped with a self-test\nsystem that may be used by connecting the unit to connector \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>R10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              :\nthis receives signals from pin 11 of connector A of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               through\nthe tester line. The self-test system also produces the signal for\nthe &quot;injection failure&quot; warning light in the instrument \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ,\nwhich comes from pin 12 of connector A of the control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives a supply\ncontrolled by the ignition (INT) at pin 15 of connector A from the\nline protected by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B11</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up to 2/99 or from fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the\nadditional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from 2/99; when this earth signal\narrives, the &quot;fuel injection fault&quot; warning light comes\non.</p><p>The speedometer signal (vehicle speed) reaches\npin 27 of connector A of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234310\">E4021</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ).</p><p>The control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               sends from pin\n2 of connector A a signal proportional to the engine rpm (\n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234270\">E4020</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ).</p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is connected to\nthe air conditioning system via pins 19 and 31 of connector A. This\nallows engine idling speed to be adjusted to increased engine load\nwhenever the compressor is activated, or to turn off the compressor in\nthe case of high speeds or high engine loads (\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234652\">E6021</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ).</p><p>The control unit also controls the engine\ncooling system: pins 4, 13, 34 and 35 of connector A control activation\nof the relevant fan  (\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234439\">E5020</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ).</p>"]]